<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    THIS ADDON RUNS ITS OWN CRON FLEET, ALONGSIDE etp_assessment_pro's.

    Both modules' crons run in the same database at the same time, and that is
    safe here because nothing is shared:

      * SEPARATE TABLES. These crons search `assessments_be_*`; upstream's
        search `etp_assessment_pro_*`. Neither can see the other's queue, so no
        row is ever processed twice and no Vertex call is ever paid for twice.
      * SEPARATE ADVISORY LOCKS. constants.py renumbers every lock into the
        8273xx-8275xx block. Sharing upstream's numbers would have made these
        crons SILENTLY starve - pg_try_advisory_lock returns false and the tick
        does nothing, with no error to see.

    So upstream keeps working untouched, and this addon drains its own work.

    NAMES ARE PREFIXED "Assessments BE v2:" ON PURPOSE. Upstream's 13 records
    are called "ETP Assessment: ..." and both fleets are active, so identical
    names would put 26 indistinguishable rows in Scheduled Actions - and the
    one operation anyone performs there is disabling a job. Disabling the wrong
    module's copy is silent and looks exactly like the right one.

    ══ PRIORITY IS NOT DECORATION. DO NOT RESET THESE TO THE DEFAULT 5. ══

    Odoo picks ready jobs with `ORDER BY failure_count, priority, id`
    (base/models/ir_cron.py, `_get_all_ready_jobs`). Every record here used to
    carry the default priority 5, so the tie broke on `id` - and the ids run in
    declaration order, which put the four Vertex-bound scoring shards (the first
    records in this file) AHEAD of `ir_cron_expire_stale_attempts`.

    That job settles a candidate's paper. Measured on the local rig, one
    `Auto-score submitted candidates` tick ran for 33.6 SECONDS while the
    per-tick median across 8,168 ticks was 0.010s. With `max_cron_threads = 1`
    - the deployed value, shared with ~49 crons from greythr, essl_server,
    kensei2, iris, lynceus and the rest - a candidate whose deadline passed
    waited behind that. Auto-submit is now priority 0 and nothing queues ahead
    of it.

    The scale, in order of who is waiting:

        0  expire_stale_attempts       a candidate's paper is being settled
        3  recompute, invitations      candidate-visible, p50 0.05-0.10s
        7  the four scoring shards     the 33.6s job; must yield to the above
        8  authoring (render, detect,  nobody waits on these mid-exam
           generate, tags, video)
        9  purge_expired_pii           daily housekeeping

    ══ THE FOUR AUTHORING JOBS RUN EVERY 5 MINUTES, NOT EVERY MINUTE ══

    render_pending_images, detect_image_labels, generate_from_sop and
    extract_tags are the ticks that can hold the single cron thread for tens of
    seconds (each makes a Vertex or imaging call). Nothing candidate-facing
    depends on their latency: an operator authoring a paper is not on a
    60-second clock. Five minutes holds the thread 5x less often.

    Left at 1 minute deliberately: expire_stale_attempts (settles papers),
    recompute_subjective_results (also re-checks outliers and closes
    finished cohorts), send_invitations,
    and the scoring shards (a grading queue that drains at cohort scale).

    ══ noupdate="1" MEANS EDITING THIS FILE DOES NOTHING TO A LIVE DATABASE ══

    Every change above is also applied by
    `migrations/19.0.3.15.0/post-migrate.py`, which is what actually reaches an
    installed database - and which also staggers `nextcall`, since 11 of these
    13 were firing in the SAME SECOND. Change one, change the other.
-->
<odoo>
    <data noupdate="1">

        <record id="ir_cron_llm_auto_score" model="ir.cron">
            <field name="name">Assessments BE v2: Auto-score submitted candidates</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="model_assessments_be"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">model._cron_llm_auto_score(shard=0)</field>
            <field name="interval_number">1</field>
            <field name="interval_type">minutes</field>
            <field name="priority">7</field>
            <field name="active" eval="True"/>
        </record>

        <!-- Parallel scoring lanes 1-3. Idle no-ops until
             ir.config_parameter assessments_be_v2.scoring_shards > shard. -->
        <record id="ir_cron_llm_auto_score_shard_1" model="ir.cron">
            <field name="name">Assessments BE v2: Auto-score (shard 1)</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="model_assessments_be"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">model._cron_llm_auto_score(shard=1)</field>
            <field name="interval_number">1</field>
            <field name="interval_type">minutes</field>
            <field name="priority">7</field>
            <field name="active" eval="True"/>
        </record>

        <record id="ir_cron_llm_auto_score_shard_2" model="ir.cron">
            <field name="name">Assessments BE v2: Auto-score (shard 2)</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="model_assessments_be"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">model._cron_llm_auto_score(shard=2)</field>
            <field name="interval_number">1</field>
            <field name="interval_type">minutes</field>
            <field name="priority">7</field>
            <field name="active" eval="True"/>
        </record>

        <record id="ir_cron_llm_auto_score_shard_3" model="ir.cron">
            <field name="name">Assessments BE v2: Auto-score (shard 3)</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="model_assessments_be"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">model._cron_llm_auto_score(shard=3)</field>
            <field name="interval_number">1</field>
            <field name="interval_type">minutes</field>
            <field name="priority">7</field>
            <field name="active" eval="True"/>
        </record>

        <record id="ir_cron_recompute_subjective_results" model="ir.cron">
            <field name="name">Assessments BE v2: Recompute pass/fail after threshold change</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="model_assessments_be"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">model._cron_recompute_subjective_results()</field>
            <field name="interval_number">1</field>
            <field name="interval_type">minutes</field>
            <field name="priority">3</field>
            <field name="active" eval="True"/>
        </record>

        <record id="ir_cron_send_pending_invitations" model="ir.cron">
            <field name="name">Assessments BE v2: Send queued candidate invitations</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="model_assessments_be_evaluator"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">model._cron_send_pending_invitations()</field>
            <field name="interval_number">1</field>
            <field name="interval_type">minutes</field>
            <field name="priority">3</field>
            <field name="active" eval="True"/>
        </record>

        <record id="ir_cron_render_pending_images" model="ir.cron">
            <field name="name">Assessments BE v2: Auto-render pending question images</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="model_assessments_be_prompt_question"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">model._cron_render_pending_images()</field>
            <field name="interval_number">5</field>
            <field name="interval_type">minutes</field>
            <field name="priority">8</field>
            <field name="active" eval="True"/>
        </record>

        <record id="ir_cron_detect_image_labels" model="ir.cron">
            <field name="name">Assessments BE v2: Detect &amp; annotate image_label images</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="model_assessments_be_question_image"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">model._cron_detect_image_labels()</field>
            <field name="interval_number">5</field>
            <field name="interval_type">minutes</field>
            <field name="priority">8</field>
            <field name="active" eval="True"/>
        </record>

        <record id="ir_cron_poll_video_ops" model="ir.cron">
            <field name="name">Assessments BE v2: Submit &amp; poll async Veo video generation</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="model_assessments_be_prompt_question"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">model._cron_poll_video_ops()</field>
            <field name="interval_number">2</field>
            <field name="interval_type">minutes</field>
            <field name="priority">8</field>
            <field name="active" eval="True"/>
        </record>

        <record id="ir_cron_expire_stale_attempts" model="ir.cron">
            <field name="name">Assessments BE v2: Auto-submit abandoned attempts past deadline</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="model_assessments_be_evaluator"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">model._cron_expire_stale_attempts()</field>
            <field name="interval_number">1</field>
            <field name="interval_type">minutes</field>
            <field name="priority">0</field>
            <field name="active" eval="True"/>
        </record>

        <record id="ir_cron_generate_from_sop" model="ir.cron">
            <field name="name">Assessments BE v2: Generate questions from SOP</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="model_assessments_be_prompt"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">model._cron_generate_from_sop()</field>
            <field name="interval_number">5</field>
            <field name="interval_type">minutes</field>
            <field name="priority">8</field>
            <field name="active" eval="True"/>
        </record>

        <!-- Drainer for tag extraction. Extraction is still MANUAL-ONLY: this
             cron never selects a generator on its own, it only picks up rows an
             admin explicitly queued by pressing Extract Tags (which fires
             _trigger() so the work starts within seconds, not on the next
             tick). The periodic interval is the crash-recovery safety net for a
             row whose trigger was lost with a killed worker.

             It must NOT run inside the web request: the request holds a
             REPEATABLE READ snapshot for the whole ~20s Vertex call, and any
             other committed write to the same prompt row makes the request's
             own final write fail with 40001. See _queue_tag_extract(). -->
        <record id="ir_cron_extract_tags" model="ir.cron">
            <field name="name">Assessments BE v2: Extract SOP tags (queued only)</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="model_assessments_be_prompt"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">model._cron_extract_tags()</field>
            <field name="interval_number">5</field>
            <field name="interval_type">minutes</field>
            <field name="priority">8</field>
            <field name="active" eval="True"/>
        </record>

        <record id="ir_cron_purge_expired_pii" model="ir.cron">
            <field name="name">Assessments BE v2: Purge expired candidate PII (retention)</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="model_assessments_be_evaluator"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">model._cron_purge_expired_pii()</field>
            <field name="interval_number">1</field>
            <field name="interval_type">days</field>
            <field name="priority">9</field>
            <field name="active" eval="True"/>
        </record>

    </data>
</odoo>
